iomat-tools
===========

Tools for interacting with the Realtek I/O Expander device:

  o iomat-update - update EC firmware over the kernel firmware_upload
                  interface (/sys/class/firmware/rts591x-ec*)
  o iomat-mem     - memory access helper over the iomatrix device node


EC firmware image
-----------------

The EC main image is installed to the rootfs at:

    /usr/share/iomat-tools/rts5979.bin

The on-disk name is kept stable so iomat-update can reference a fixed
path.  Each time the EC image is updated, the new bin is tracked in this
repository by its upload date.  Replace rts5979.bin and add a row below.


Version history
---------------

Bins are identified by upload date.

2026-09-01
    - Add IO expander I2C slave protocol, GPIO table init, I2C master
      interrupt module (oem_i2cm), and ERRLOG region
    - Add peripheral event callbacks and interrupt status bits for ADC,
      TACHO, I2C master, and ACPI IBF
    - Add GPIO interrupt report (EC GPIO state changes can be reported
      for host/SoC monitoring)
    - Add in-band EC flash update from SoC (iomat-update flashes via the
      firmware_upload interface)
    - Enhance iomatrix services: PECI OOB forwarding, Port80 interrupt
      forwarding to the snoop channel, PM IBF interrupt bits
    - Align iomatrix protocol stack with Linux: KCS state machine now
      driven by IBF interrupt forwarding, IRQ bitmap aligned
    - Fix: restore LDN UART after eSPI reset


Usage
-----

Update EC firmware with the installed image (also the default when no
image is given):

    iomat-update

Update EC firmware with an image at a specified path:

    iomat-update path/image.bin

The tool auto-detects a single rts591x-ec* firmware_upload device; use
-d to select one when more than one exists.  See 'iomat-update --help'
for details.
